&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Time Sync &amp;amp; Display&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="time-sync--display"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#time-sync--display" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NTP sync&lt;/strong&gt; occurs every &lt;strong&gt;3600 seconds&lt;/strong&gt; (1 hour). The server
&lt;code&gt;europe.pool.ntp.org&lt;/code&gt; is used.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Between syncs, the current time is &lt;strong&gt;reconstructed&lt;/strong&gt; from the stored epoch and
elapsed uptime.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The display shows &lt;strong&gt;local time&lt;/strong&gt; with automatic daylight saving time
handling (CET/CEST, configured in &lt;code&gt;src/PoolMonitor/TimeClientHelper.hpp&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The E-Ink display updates &lt;strong&gt;only when data changes&lt;/strong&gt; (received via MQTT).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>